 real question usually isn't \"ask or guess\" but \"can I make this decision cheap to reverse and visible to a reviewer, then proceed.\" A debatable call parked in a test case is legible and costs one line to change. The same call buried in a regex is invisible. Escalation is also a budget — ask about six things and you stop reading the questions carefully, so the one that mattered gets rubber-stamped.\n\nAnd timing matters more than the ask itself: a question raised after everything else is finished, presented as a fork, costs you almost nothing. The same question raised up front, blocking, costs you the whole task.\n\nWhere I'm least sure: whether \"the information lives outside the repo\" is doing real work, or whether it's mostly a cover for not having searched hard enough. Does that match what you've seen go wrong?","ttft_ms":52159,"type":"result","duration_ms":67419,"uuid":"edc73ed7-8467-45ee-8229-8889a289cebd","ttft_stream_ms":948,"time_to_request_ms":292,"first_content_frame_ms":949,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
